{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgV8q4eP7orhFQnZKNX1A", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01AYokY1eKK5n68vYoZAhav5", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to orders (`0.0825`, i.e. 8.25%).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for a single line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples, sums the line totals,\n  applies `TAX_RATE`, and returns the result rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the order total minus the refunded amount.\n  It does not validate that `amount` is not larger than the order total.\n\n### Example\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # (20.00 + 5.50) * 1.0825 = 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 10.00)              # 17.6\n```\nEOF\nawk 'length>=100' README.md; python3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import *\nt=order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]);print(t,refund(t,10))\""}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 476, "cache_read_input_tokens": 38148, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 476}, "output_tokens": 20, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T18:49:16.715Z", "request_id": "req_011CgV8q4DqLXgXsNjDuDHEp", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01AYokY1eKK5n68vYoZAhav5": {"command": "cd /tmp/skilldiff-sh0wdc_v/ws && cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Payments module\n\n`shop/payments.py` computes order totals and refunds.\n\n- `TAX_RATE`: sales tax rate applied to orders (`0.0825`, i.e. 8.25%).\n- `line_total(price, quantity)`: returns `price * quantity` for a single line.\n- `order_total(lines)`: takes a list of `(price, quantity)` tuples, sums the line totals,\n  applies `TAX_RATE`, and returns the result rounded to 2 decimal places.\n- `refund(order_total_amount, amount)`: returns the order total minus the refunded amount.\n  It does not validate that `amount` is not larger than the order total.\n\n### Example\n\n```python\nfrom shop.payments import order_total, refund\n\ntotal = order_total([(10.00, 2), (5.50, 1)])  # (20.00 + 5.50) * 1.0825 = 27.6\nremaining = refund(total, 10.00)              # 17.6\n```\nEOF\nawk 'length>=100' README.md; python3 -c \"\nfrom shop.payments import *\nt=order_total([(10.00,2),(5.50,1)]);print(t,refund(t,10))\""}}, "wire_ingest_context": {"toolu_01AYokY1eKK5n68vYoZAhav5": {"cwd": "/tmp/skilldiff-sh0wdc_v/ws"}}}
